# A non-generic class whose explicit instance variables are generic instances of the prelude's Array:
# `@items : Array(Entry)` is assigned `[] of Entry` in initialize. The own-source dump must print the
# instance's argument, `Array(Entry)`, never the unbound `Array(T)`. This is the shape of compiler.iyi's
# `@resolved_modules : Array(ModuleInfo)`, which printed unbound until the own-source load gave the
# declaration pass its type system (NEEDS.md row 22). `@label : String?` is a reference union, which
# lowers to one pointer; the dump pins that too.
class Entry
end

class Index
  @items : Array(Entry)
  @names : Array(String)
  @label : String?

  def initialize
    @items = [] of Entry
    @names = [] of String
    @label = nil
  end
end
